6\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke=\"#2f8a5b\" stroke-width=\"0\"/><text x=\"151.0\" y=\"209.5\" font-size=\"9.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">10.0</text><rect x=\"144\" y=\"212\" width=\"2.0\" height=\"6\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#7a7468\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"151.0\" y=\"217.5\" font-size=\"9.5\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#1e1d1a\">10.1</text><line x1=\"144\" x2=\"612\" y1=\"236\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#e3ddd1\"/><text x=\"144\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\">10 (Low pole)</text><text x=\"378.0\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30 (Midpoint)</text><text x=\"612\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#655f55\" text-anchor=\"end\">50 (High pole)</text></svg></div><figcaption>Gemini scores near the top of the Conscientiousness pole (48.3–49.4) and sits right on the 10.0 floor of the Neuroticism axis.</figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "What the scores describe.",
      "html": "<p>Among the four May Big Five cohorts, Gemini recorded the highest Conscientiousness (48.3) and lowest Neuroticism (10.1). Those totals summarize how Gemini answered human personality items—not whether it is more accurate, calmer, or less warm on real tasks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "What we have not done.",
      "html": "<p>Gemini was not included in the September 2026 fresh-session study. If you want to test current Gemini models under our blind protocol, all five questionnaires and scoring keys are open-source at <a href=\"/tests/\">/tests/</a>, and the verification script is linked on the <a href=\"/research/ai-personality-five-models-2026\">five-model study page</a>.</p><p>Remember that human questionnaires do not measure task accuracy or prove that a personality prompt improves answers. See our <a href=\"/research#methodology\">methodology and limits</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Trying communication preferences.",
      "html": "<p>Want to adjust how Gemini responds? Read our step-by-step <a href=\"/guides/gemini-personality\">How to change Google Gemini’s personality guide</a> covering Saved Info, custom Gems, and <code>GEMINI.md</code>. You can also pick any profile in the <a href=\"/library/\">tuning library</a>, select <strong>Any model</strong> → <strong>Gemini Gems</strong>, and test the rules on your own prompts.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What MBTI type is Gemini?",
      "a": "INTJ. In the May 2026 report, Gemini 3.1 Pro scored INTJ in all 100 scoring records and called itself 'The Architect' unprompted. It has not yet been re-tested under the September 2026 fresh-session protocol."
    },
    {
      "q": "What Enneagram type is Gemini?",
      "a": "Type 1 (The Reformer) came first in 65 of 100 May 2026 records, with Type 5 (The Investigator) second. Gemini was the only model in that collection with Type 1 on top."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is Gemini securely attached?",
      "a": "Gemini 3.1 Pro scored in the Secure quadrant (anxiety 1.86, avoidance 1.62) across all 100 May records. Those numbers reflect answers to a human relationship quiz, not human attachment."
    },
    {
      "q": "How does Gemini compare with Claude and ChatGPT?",
      "a": "In the May four-model table, Gemini had the highest Conscientiousness (48.3) and lowest Neuroticism (10.1). Because collection methods differed and Gemini was not in the September fresh-session cohort, treat this as a descriptive summary rather than a ranking."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can you change Gemini's personality?",
      "a": "Yes. Add plain-English tone rules in Gemini Saved Info, a custom Gem, or a project GEMINI.md file, then verify the replies on your own tasks."
    }
  ],
